IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`

-- LAYER 1, regulation 29: additional customer due diligence measures for credit institutions and financial institutions.
-- (Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017.)
-- The text is a plain-text rendering made by a converter script; it is not the official text.
--
-- THE SHAPE.  Regulation 29 applies "in addition to regulation 28 where a relevant person is a credit institution or a financial institution" (29(1)).
-- Each duty is two functions: an "engaged" function (`... the relevant person must ...`: does the duty bind on these facts?) and a checklist
-- (`... the relevant person has ...`: on the stated facts has the requirement been met?).  A gate or case worded "where", "when" or "if" that is not met
-- answers JUST FALSE (ruling 2026-11-05, (b); fork F-when); a scope limit with no "only" answers NOTHING (ruling 2026-11-05, (c)); the "may" form of a prohibition
-- answers NOTHING when its condition is not met (fork F-polarity); a flat negative ("must not", "may not", "is not
-- required") answers JUST FALSE for the act it forbids or the duty it removes.  Whether regulation 29(1) governs paragraphs (6) to (9) as well as the
-- insurance and pooled-account paragraphs is read as the structure of the regulation has it: it does (Marginal readings, (g)).

§ `Regulation 29(1) and (2) -- Where the regulation applies`

-- reg 29(1).  This regulation applies in addition to regulation 28 where a relevant person is a credit institution or a financial institution.
-- src:878 | (1) This regulation applies in addition to regulation 28 where a relevant person is a credit institution or a financial institution.
@ref reg 29(1) (src:878-878)
GIVEN `the kinds of the relevant person` IS A LIST OF `Kind of relevant person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 29(1) this regulation applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem `credit institution` `the kinds of the relevant person` OR elem `financial institution` `the kinds of the relevant person` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This regulation applies in addition to regulation 28 where a relevant person is a credit institution or a financial institution" (Ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met)

-- reg 29(2).  Paragraphs (3) to (5) apply if the relevant person is providing a customer with a contract of long-term insurance ("the insurance policy").
-- SEAM S-K4 (asking): the keel's regulation 3(1) answers whether the contract is a contract of long-term insurance.
-- src:879 | (2) Paragraphs (3) to (5) apply if the relevant person is providing a customer with a contract of long-term insurance (“the insurance policy”).
@ref reg 29(2) (src:879-879)
GIVEN `reg 3(1) the contract is a contract of long-term insurance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person is providing a customer with that contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 29(2) paragraphs (3) to (5) apply` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the relevant person is providing a customer with that contract`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraphs (3) to (5) apply if the relevant person is providing a customer with a contract of long-term insurance" (Marginal readings, (a): a failed condition of an "if")
        IF `reg 3(1) the contract is a contract of long-term insurance` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `reg 3(1) the contract is a contract of long-term insurance` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the relevant person is providing a customer with a contract of long-term insurance" (Marginal readings, (a): the contract is not one of long-term insurance)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): regulation 3(1) has not answered whether the contract is a contract of long-term insurance

§ `Regulation 29(3) to (5) -- Beneficiaries of an insurance policy`

-- reg 29(3).  As soon as the beneficiaries of the insurance policy are identified or designated, the relevant person must (a) if the beneficiary is a
-- named person or legal arrangement, take the full name of the person or arrangement; or (b) if the beneficiaries are designated by specified
-- characteristics, as a class or in any other way, obtain sufficient information about the beneficiaries to satisfy itself that it will be able to
-- establish the identity of the beneficiary before any payment is made under the insurance policy.
