        IF NOT (`reg 29(2) paragraphs (3) to (5) apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "reg 29(2) paragraphs (3) to (5) apply" has not been answered
        IF NOT (`the relevant person becomes aware that all or part of the rights under the insurance policy are being, or have been, assigned to an individual, body corporate, trust or other legal arrangement which is receiving the value or part of the value of the insurance policy for its own benefit`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the relevant person becomes aware that all or part of the rights under the insurance policy are being, or have been, assigned to an individual, body corporate, trust or other legal arrangement which is receiving the value or part of the value of the insurance policy for its own benefit" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; "when", "upon", "whenever" read as "where", fork F-when)
