§ `Regulation 29(6) to (9) -- Anonymous accounts and open-ended investment companies`

DECLARE `reg 29 party` IS ONE OF
    `reg 29 the relevant person`

DECLARE `reg 29 act` IS ONE OF
    `reg 29(6) set up an anonymous account, an anonymous passbook or an anonymous safe-deposit box`
    `reg 29(8) issue shares evidenced by a share certificate or other documentary evidence of entitlement`

-- reg 29(6).  The relevant person must not set up an anonymous account, an anonymous passbook or an anonymous safe-deposit box for any new or existing
-- customer.
-- src:885 | (6) The relevant person must not set up an anonymous account, an anonymous passbook or an anonymous safe-deposit box for any new or existing customer.
@ref reg 29(6) (src:885-885)
GIVEN `reg 29(1) this regulation applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 29(6) the relevant person may set up an anonymous account, an anonymous passbook or an anonymous safe-deposit box for a new or existing customer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 29(1) this regulation applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The relevant person must not set up an anonymous account, an anonymous passbook or an anonymous safe-deposit box for any new or existing customer"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This regulation applies in addition to regulation 28 where a relevant person is a credit institution or a financial institution" (permission form of a prohibition, fork F-polarity: an unmet condition says nothing about whether the person may)

-- The same prohibition as a regulative rule (ruling N2: the SHANT is derived from the flat negative).  The text gives no time limit and none is
-- invented: an act is a breach; with no act the prohibition stands.
`reg 29(6) the prohibition on setting up an anonymous account, passbook or safe-deposit box` MEANS
    PARTY `reg 29 the relevant person`
    SHANT `reg 29(6) set up an anonymous account, an anonymous passbook or an anonymous safe-deposit box`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `reg 29 the relevant person` BECAUSE "the relevant person set up an anonymous account, an anonymous passbook or an anonymous safe-deposit box"

#TRACE `reg 29(6) the prohibition on setting up an anonymous account, passbook or safe-deposit box` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `reg 29 the relevant person` DOES `reg 29(6) set up an anonymous account, an anonymous passbook or an anonymous safe-deposit box` AT 5

#TRACE `reg 29(6) the prohibition on setting up an anonymous account, passbook or safe-deposit box` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 5)

-- reg 29(7).  The relevant person must apply customer due diligence measures to all anonymous accounts and passbooks in existence on the date on which these
-- Regulations come into force, and in any event before such accounts or passbooks are used in any way.
-- src:886 | (7) The relevant person must apply customer due diligence measures to all anonymous accounts and passbooks in existence on the date on which these Regulations come into force, and in any event before such accounts or passbooks are used in any way.
@ref reg 29(7) (src:886-886)
GIVEN `reg 29(1) this regulation applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the anonymous account or passbook was in existence on the date on which these Regulations come into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 29(7) the relevant person must apply customer due diligence measures to the anonymous account or passbook` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 29(1) this regulation applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This regulation applies in addition to regulation 28 where a relevant person is a credit institution or a financial institution" (assumed 2026-11-05, fork F-when: "when" read as "where"; ruling (b): a "where" condition not met)
        IF NOT (`reg 29(1) this regulation applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "reg 29(1) this regulation applies" has not been answered
        IF NOT (`the anonymous account or passbook was in existence on the date on which these Regulations come into force`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the anonymous account or passbook was in existence on the date on which these Regulations come into force" (ruling 2026-11-05, (c): a scope limit with no "only")
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref reg 29(7) (src:886-886)
GIVEN `it has applied customer due diligence measures to the anonymous account or passbook` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it did so before the account or passbook was used in any way` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 29(7) the relevant person has applied customer due diligence measures to the anonymous account or passbook` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has applied customer due diligence measures to the anonymous account or passbook` AND `it did so before the account or passbook was used in any way` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and in any event before such accounts or passbooks are used in any way" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 29(7A).  The relevant person must apply customer due diligence measures to all anonymous safe-deposit boxes in existence on 10th January 2019,
-- and in any event before such safe-deposit boxes are used in any way.
-- src:887 | (7A) The relevant person must apply customer due diligence measures to all anonymous safe-deposit boxes in existence on 10th January 2019, and in any event before such safe-deposit boxes are used in any way.
@ref reg 29(7A) (src:887-887)
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 29(7A) the date of 10th January 2019` MEANS Date 10 1 2019

-- src:887 | (7A) The relevant person must apply customer due diligence measures to all anonymous safe-deposit boxes in existence on 10th January 2019, and in any event before such safe-deposit boxes are used in any way.
@ref reg 29(7A) (src:887-887)
