    BRANCH
        IF `reg 29(1) this regulation applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This regulation applies in addition to regulation 28 where a relevant person is a credit institution or a financial institution" (assumed 2026-11-05, fork F-when: "when" read as "where"; ruling (b): a "where" condition not met)
        IF NOT (`reg 29(1) this regulation applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "reg 29(1) this regulation applies" has not been answered
        IF NOT (`the anonymous safe-deposit box was in existence on 10th January 2019`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the anonymous safe-deposit box was in existence on 10th January 2019" (ruling 2026-11-05, (c): a scope limit with no "only")
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref reg 29(7A) (src:887-887)
GIVEN `it has applied customer due diligence measures to the anonymous safe-deposit box` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it did so before the safe-deposit box was used in any way` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 29(7A) the relevant person has applied customer due diligence measures to the anonymous safe-deposit box` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has applied customer due diligence measures to the anonymous safe-deposit box` AND `it did so before the safe-deposit box was used in any way` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and in any event before such safe-deposit boxes are used in any way" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 29(9).  Paragraph (8) does not apply to an open-ended investment company if (a) an application for an authorisation order under regulation 12 of
-- the Open-ended Investment Companies Regulations 2001 was made in relation to that open-ended investment company before the date on which these
-- Regulations come into force; and (b) that application was not determined until a date on or after the date on which these Regulations come into force.
-- src:892 | (9) Paragraph (8) does not apply to an open-ended investment company if—
-- src:893 | (a) an application for an authorisation order under regulation 12 of the Open-ended Investment Companies Regulations 2001 was made in relation to that open-ended investment company before the date on which these Regulations come into force; and
-- src:894 | (b) that application was not determined until a date on or after the date on which these Regulations come into force.
@ref reg 29(9) (src:892-894)
GIVEN `the date on which the application for an authorisation order under regulation 12 of the Open-ended Investment Companies Regulations 2001 was made` IS A DATE
      `the date on which that application was determined` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 29(9) paragraph (8) does not apply to the open-ended investment company` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (Day `the date on which the application for an authorisation order under regulation 12 of the Open-ended Investment Companies Regulations 2001 was made`) MINUS (Day `reg 1(2) the date these Regulations came into force`) LESS THAN 0 AND (Day `the date on which that application was determined`) MINUS (Day `reg 1(2) the date these Regulations came into force`) AT LEAST 0 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (8) does not apply to an open-ended investment company if— (a) an application ... was made ... before the date on which these Regulations come into force; and (b) that application was not determined until a date on or after the date on which these Regulations come into force" (Marginal readings, (a): a failed condition of an "if")

-- reg 29(8).  A relevant person which (a) is an open-ended investment company within the meaning of regulation 2(1) of the Open-Ended Investment Companies
-- Regulations 2001; and (b) is authorised on or after the date on which these Regulations come into force, may not issue shares evidenced by a share
-- certificate (or any other documentary evidence) indicating that the holder of the certificate or document is entitled to the shares specified in it.
-- src:888 | (8) A relevant person which—
-- src:889 | (a) is an open-ended investment company within the meaning of regulation 2(1) of the Open-Ended Investment Companies Regulations 2001 ; and
-- src:890 | (b) is authorised on or after the date on which these Regulations come into force,
-- src:891 | may not issue shares evidenced by a share certificate (or any other documentary evidence) indicating that the holder of the certificate or document is entitled to the shares specified in it.
@ref reg 29(8) (src:888-891)
GIVEN `reg 29(1) this regulation applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person is an open-ended investment company within the meaning of regulation 2(1) of the Open-Ended Investment Companies Regulations 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the relevant person is authorised` IS A DATE
      `reg 29(9) paragraph (8) does not apply to the open-ended investment company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 29(8) the relevant person may issue shares evidenced by a share certificate or other documentary evidence of entitlement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`reg 29(1) this regulation applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This regulation applies in addition to regulation 28 where a relevant person is a credit institution or a financial institution" (permission form of a prohibition, fork F-polarity: an unmet condition says nothing about whether the person may)
        IF NOT (`the relevant person is an open-ended investment company within the meaning of regulation 2(1) of the Open-Ended Investment Companies Regulations 2001`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A relevant person which (a) is an open-ended investment company" (permission form of a prohibition, fork F-polarity: an unmet condition says nothing about whether the person may)
        IF (Day `the date on which the relevant person is authorised`) MINUS (Day `reg 1(2) the date these Regulations came into force`) LESS THAN 0 THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) is authorised on or after the date on which these Regulations come into force" (permission form of a prohibition, fork F-polarity: an unmet condition says nothing about whether the person may)
        IF `reg 29(9) paragraph (8) does not apply to the open-ended investment company` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (9) takes the company out of paragraph (8), and the text then says nothing about issuing share certificates (permission form of a prohibition, fork F-polarity: an unmet condition says nothing about whether the person may)
        IF `reg 29(9) paragraph (8) does not apply to the open-ended investment company` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether paragraph (9) applies has not been answered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not issue shares evidenced by a share certificate (or any other documentary evidence) indicating that the holder of the certificate or document is entitled to the shares specified in it"

`reg 29(8) the prohibition on issuing shares evidenced by a share certificate` MEANS
    PARTY `reg 29 the relevant person`
    SHANT `reg 29(8) issue shares evidenced by a share certificate or other documentary evidence of entitlement`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `reg 29 the relevant person` BECAUSE "the relevant person issued shares evidenced by a share certificate or other documentary evidence of entitlement"

#TRACE `reg 29(8) the prohibition on issuing shares evidenced by a share certificate` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `reg 29 the relevant person` DOES `reg 29(8) issue shares evidenced by a share certificate or other documentary evidence of entitlement` AT 5

#TRACE `reg 29(8) the prohibition on issuing shares evidenced by a share certificate` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 5)

§ `Regulation 29(10) to (18) -- Pooled accounts`

-- reg 29(10).  Paragraphs (11) to (17) apply if the relevant person provides a customer with a new account into which monies are pooled ("pooled account")
-- on or after the day on which this paragraph comes into force.
-- The text does not say the day on which paragraph (10) comes into force; it is a DATE input (fork F-29(10) in NOTES).
-- src:895 | (10) Paragraphs (11) to (17) apply if the relevant person provides a customer with a new account into which monies are pooled (“pooled account”) on or after the day on which this paragraph comes into force.
@ref reg 29(10) (src:895-895)
GIVEN `the relevant person provides a customer with a new account into which monies are pooled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the relevant person provides the customer with the account` IS A DATE
      `the day on which paragraph (10) comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 29(10) paragraphs (11) to (17) apply` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the relevant person provides a customer with a new account into which monies are pooled` AND (Day `the date on which the relevant person provides the customer with the account`) MINUS (Day `the day on which paragraph (10) comes into force`) AT LEAST 0 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraphs (11) to (17) apply if the relevant person provides a customer with a new account into which monies are pooled ... on or after the day on which this paragraph comes into force" (Marginal readings, (a): a failed condition of an "if")

-- reg 29(11).  When providing a customer with a pooled account, the relevant person must (a) take reasonable measures to understand the purpose of the
-- pooled account and how the customer proposes to use it; (b) take steps to be satisfied that the purpose and proposed use under sub-paragraph (a) is
-- consistent with the relevant person's knowledge of the customer, the customer's business and risk profile, and must conduct updated customer due
-- diligence measures where it is not so satisfied; and (c) once satisfied under sub-paragraph (b), assess the level of risk of money laundering and
-- terrorist financing associated with the customer using the pooled account and take reasonable steps to manage and mitigate the risks arising from that
-- use by the customer.
-- src:896 | (11) When providing a customer with a pooled account, the relevant person must—
-- src:897 | (a) take reasonable measures to understand the purpose of the pooled account and how the customer proposes to use it;
-- src:898 | (b) take steps to be satisfied that the purpose and proposed use under sub-paragraph (a) is consistent with the relevant person’s knowledge of the customer, the customer’s business and risk profile, and must conduct updated customer due diligence measures where it is not so satisfied; and
-- src:899 | (c) once satisfied under sub-paragraph (b), assess the level of risk of money laundering and terrorist financing associated with the customer using the pooled account and take reasonable steps to manage and mitigate the risks arising from that use by the customer.
@ref reg 29(11) (src:896-899)
GIVEN `reg 29(1) this regulation applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 29(10) paragraphs (11) to (17) apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 29(11) the relevant person must take the steps that paragraph (11) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 29(1) this regulation applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This regulation applies in addition to regulation 28 where a relevant person is a credit institution or a financial institution" (assumed 2026-11-05, fork F-when: "when" read as "where"; ruling (b): a "where" condition not met)
        IF NOT (`reg 29(1) this regulation applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "reg 29(1) this regulation applies" has not been answered
        IF `reg 29(10) paragraphs (11) to (17) apply` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraphs (11) to (17) apply if the relevant person provides a customer with a new account into which monies are pooled (“pooled account”) on or after the day on which this paragraph comes into force" (Marginal readings, (a): a failed condition of an "if")
        IF NOT (`reg 29(10) paragraphs (11) to (17) apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "reg 29(10) paragraphs (11) to (17) apply" has not been answered
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref reg 29(11) (src:897-899)
GIVEN `it has taken reasonable measures to understand the purpose of the pooled account and how the customer proposes to use it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken steps to be satisfied that the purpose and proposed use is consistent with its knowledge of the customer, the customer's business and risk profile, and where it is not so satisfied it has conducted updated customer due diligence measures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `once satisfied, it has assessed the level of risk of money laundering and terrorist financing associated with the customer using the pooled account and taken reasonable steps to manage and mitigate the risks arising from that use by the customer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 29(11) the relevant person has taken the steps that paragraph (11) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has taken reasonable measures to understand the purpose of the pooled account and how the customer proposes to use it` AND `it has taken steps to be satisfied that the purpose and proposed use is consistent with its knowledge of the customer, the customer's business and risk profile, and where it is not so satisfied it has conducted updated customer due diligence measures` AND `once satisfied, it has assessed the level of risk of money laundering and terrorist financing associated with the customer using the pooled account and taken reasonable steps to manage and mitigate the risks arising from that use by the customer` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When providing a customer with a pooled account, the relevant person must—" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 29(12).  In making an assessment under paragraph (11)(c), the relevant person must consider, among other things, the appropriateness of imposing
-- controls on the pooled account to manage and mitigate the risks.
-- src:900 | (12) In making an assessment under paragraph (11)(c), the relevant person must consider, among other things, the appropriateness of imposing controls on the pooled account to manage and mitigate the risks.
@ref reg 29(12) (src:900-900)
GIVEN `it has considered the appropriateness of imposing controls on the pooled account to manage and mitigate the risks` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person is making an assessment under paragraph (11)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 29(12) the relevant person has considered the appropriateness of imposing controls on the pooled account` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the relevant person is making an assessment under paragraph (11)(c)`) THEN JUST TRUE -- the duty does not arise: "the relevant person is making an assessment under paragraph (11)(c)" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; in a function that asks whether the requirement has been met, a duty that does not arise leaves nothing unmet, as in the "unless" of reg 18(4) and reg 21(3); fork F-where)
        IF `it has considered the appropriateness of imposing controls on the pooled account to manage and mitigate the risks` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In making an assessment under paragraph (11)(c), the relevant person must consider, among other things, the appropriateness of imposing controls on the pooled account to manage and mitigate the risks" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 29(13).  The relevant person must be able to demonstrate to its supervisory authority that the extent of the measures it has taken to satisfy the
-- requirements under paragraphs (11) and (12) is appropriate in view of the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing.
-- src:901 | (13) The relevant person must be able to demonstrate to its supervisory authority that the extent of the measures it has taken to satisfy the requirements under paragraphs (11) and (12) is appropriate in view of the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing.
@ref reg 29(13) (src:901-901)
GIVEN `it is able to demonstrate to its supervisory authority that the extent of the measures it has taken to satisfy the requirements under paragraphs (11) and (12) is appropriate in view of the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 29(13) the relevant person is able to demonstrate to its supervisory authority that the extent of the measures is appropriate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is able to demonstrate to its supervisory authority that the extent of the measures it has taken to satisfy the requirements under paragraphs (11) and (12) is appropriate in view of the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The relevant person must be able to demonstrate to its supervisory authority that the extent of the measures it has taken to satisfy the requirements under paragraphs (11) and (12) is appropriate in view of the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 29(17).  A customer is not required under paragraph (13), (14) or (16) to provide information which that person would be entitled to refuse to
-- provide on grounds of legal professional privilege in proceedings in the High Court (or, in Scotland, on the ground of confidentiality of
-- communications in the Court of Session).
-- The text names paragraph (13), which lays a duty on the relevant person and not on a customer (NOTES, "What the text turns out to say").
-- src:905 | (17) A customer is not required under paragraph (13), (14) or (16) to provide information which that person would be entitled to refuse to provide on grounds of legal professional privilege in proceedings in the High Court (or, in Scotland, on the ground of confidentiality of communications in the Court of Session).
@ref reg 29(17) (src:905-905)
GIVEN `the information is information which the customer would be entitled to refuse to provide on grounds of legal professional privilege in proceedings in the High Court, or in Scotland on the ground of confidentiality of communications in the Court of Session` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 29(17) the customer is required under paragraph (13), (14) or (16) to provide the information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the information is information which the customer would be entitled to refuse to provide on grounds of legal professional privilege in proceedings in the High Court, or in Scotland on the ground of confidentiality of communications in the Court of Session` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A customer is not required under paragraph (13), (14) or (16) to provide information which that person would be entitled to refuse to provide on grounds of legal professional privilege"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph removes the requirement for privileged information and says nothing of other information (exception polarity, fork F-polarity: the function asks the question the exception answers no to, so an unmet condition leaves that question to the rest of the Regulations)

-- reg 29(14).  When a customer has a pooled account with a relevant person, the customer must make available to the relevant person, on request from the
-- relevant person, information on the identity of the persons on whose behalf monies are held in the pooled account and information on the identity of
-- any beneficial owners of those persons.
-- src:902 | (14) When a customer has a pooled account with a relevant person, the customer must make available to the relevant person, on request from the relevant person, information on the identity of the persons on whose behalf monies are held in the pooled account and information on the identity of any beneficial owners of those persons.
@ref reg 29(14) (src:902-902)
GIVEN `reg 29(10) paragraphs (11) to (17) apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the customer has a pooled account with a relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person has requested the information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is privileged: the customer would be entitled to refuse to provide it on grounds of legal professional privilege` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 29(14) the customer must make information on the persons on whose behalf monies are held available to the relevant person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 29(10) paragraphs (11) to (17) apply` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraphs (11) to (17) apply if the relevant person provides a customer with a new account into which monies are pooled (“pooled account”) on or after the day on which this paragraph comes into force" (Marginal readings, (a): a failed condition of an "if")
        IF NOT (`reg 29(10) paragraphs (11) to (17) apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "reg 29(10) paragraphs (11) to (17) apply" has not been answered
        IF NOT (`the customer has a pooled account with a relevant person`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the customer has a pooled account with a relevant person" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; "when", "upon", "whenever" read as "where", fork F-when)
        IF NOT (`the relevant person has requested the information`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the relevant person has requested the information" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; "when", "upon", "whenever" read as "where", fork F-when)
        IF `the information is privileged: the customer would be entitled to refuse to provide it on grounds of legal professional privilege` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A customer is not required under paragraph (13), (14) or (16) to provide information which that person would be entitled to refuse to provide on grounds of legal professional privilege in proceedings in the High Court (or, in Scotland, on the ground of confidentiality of communications in the Court of Session)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref reg 29(14) (src:902-902)
GIVEN `it has made available to the relevant person information on the identity of the persons on whose behalf monies are held in the pooled account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has made available to the relevant person information on the identity of any beneficial owners of those persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 29(14) the customer has made the information available to the relevant person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has made available to the relevant person information on the identity of the persons on whose behalf monies are held in the pooled account` AND `it has made available to the relevant person information on the identity of any beneficial owners of those persons` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the customer must make available to the relevant person, on request from the relevant person, information on the identity of the persons on whose behalf monies are held" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 29(15).  A customer which is provided with a pooled account by a relevant person must maintain accurate and up-to-date records in writing of all the
-- monies that are paid into and out of the pooled account for a period of five years beginning, in the case of each payment into or out of the account, on
-- the date on which the customer knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that the payment is complete.
-- The period of five years beginning on a date ends on the day before the fifth anniversary of that date (Marginal readings, (d)); a 29 February start
-- has no anniversary in a common year, and `Date` rolls it forward to 1 March (NOTES, Dependencies).
-- src:903 | (15) A customer which is provided with a pooled account by a relevant person must maintain accurate and up-to-date records in writing of all the monies that are paid into and out of the pooled account for a period of five years beginning, in the case of each payment into or out of the account, on the date on which the customer knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that the payment is complete.
@ref reg 29(15) (src:903-903)
GIVEN `reg 29(10) paragraphs (11) to (17) apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 29(15) the customer must maintain accurate and up-to-date records in writing of the monies paid into and out of the pooled account` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 29(10) paragraphs (11) to (17) apply` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraphs (11) to (17) apply if the relevant person provides a customer with a new account into which monies are pooled (“pooled account”) on or after the day on which this paragraph comes into force" (Marginal readings, (a): a failed condition of an "if")
        IF NOT (`reg 29(10) paragraphs (11) to (17) apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "reg 29(10) paragraphs (11) to (17) apply" has not been answered
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref reg 29(15) (src:903-903)
GIVEN `the date on which the customer knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that the payment is complete` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 29(15) the fifth anniversary of the date on which the payment is complete` MEANS
    Date (DATE_DAY `the date on which the customer knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that the payment is complete`) (DATE_MONTH `the date on which the customer knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that the payment is complete`) ((DATE_YEAR `the date on which the customer knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that the payment is complete`) PLUS 5)

@ref reg 29(15) (src:903-903)
GIVEN `the date on which the customer knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that the payment is complete` IS A DATE
      `the last day on which the customer maintained the records of that payment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 29(15) the customer maintained the records of the payment for the whole period of five years` MEANS
    (Day `the last day on which the customer maintained the records of that payment`) MINUS (Day (`reg 29(15) the fifth anniversary of the date on which the payment is complete` `the date on which the customer knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that the payment is complete`)) AT LEAST (0 MINUS 1)

