        IF `the information is privileged: the customer would be entitled to refuse to provide it on grounds of legal professional privilege` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A customer is not required under paragraph (13), (14) or (16) to provide information which that person would be entitled to refuse to provide on grounds of legal professional privilege in proceedings in the High Court (or, in Scotland, on the ground of confidentiality of communications in the Court of Session)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref reg 29(16) (src:904-904)
GIVEN `it has provided to the law enforcement authority information about itself and the management and use of any pooled account it has with the relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
